new file mode 100644
index 0000000..061be2f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/mermaid/src/docs/syntax/contour.md
@@ -0,0 +1,206 @@
+---
+description: 'Draw every AI use of an organisation as one mark with seven dimensions, in six standard views, with the contour-beta diagram.'
+---
+
+<!-- cspell:ignore Nordqvist -->
+
+# Contour Diagram (beta)
+
+> **Warning**
+> Contour is a beta diagram. Its syntax is introduced with the `contour-beta` keyword and may change before it is declared stable.
+
+## Introduction
+
+Contour is a notation for the landscape that emerges in an organisation when AI tools go to work. It draws every AI use, called a **unit**, as one **mark** with seven dimensions, so that a whole organisation fits on one page and two organisations can be compared at identical scales. The diagram is written as text, one `unit` line per AI use, and drawn the same way every time.
+
+Contour was designed for the book _Landscape: A Fact-Based Picture of Architecture and AI at Work_ by Gunnar Nordqvist. The notation is specified in that book; this page documents only the diagram type.
+
+## The seven dimensions
+
+| Dimension     | Drawn as                                            | Attribute and values                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |
+| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Autonomy      | Column                                              | `level=0` to `level=4`: Level 0 Advisory, Level 1 Assisted, Level 2 Supervised, Level 3 Bounded, Level 4 Autonomous                                                                                                                                                                    |
+| Reversibility | Row                                                 | `rev=R1` to `rev=R4`: R1 Reversible at once, R2 Reversible with effort, R3 Hard to reverse, R4 Irreversible                                                                                                                                                                            |
+| Reach         | Size                                                | `reach=S`, `M`, `L`, `XL`: the number of people the unit's actions touch in a year (S under 100, M 100 to 999, L 1,000 to 9,999, XL 10,000 and more)                                                                                                                                   |
+| Usage mode    | Colour, with the mode number in the mark            | `mode=0` to `mode=5`: Ambient AI, Conversational assistants, Embedded workplace assistants, Agentic work tools, Built AI applications, Autonomous production agents                                                                                                                    |
+| Identity      | Shape                                               | `identity=person` (circle: acts with a person's identity) or `identity=own` (rounded square: acts with an identity of its own)                                                                                                                                                         |
+| Control       | A diamond (policy point) and a seat carrying a tier | `policy=enforced` (filled diamond), `planned` (hollow diamond) or `none`; `tier=T1` to `T4` for the person who holds the decision right (T1 operator or user, T2 system owner or architect, T3 executive, T4 board or elected body); `T0` means nobody is named and the seat is absent |
+| Evidence      | A baseline under the mark                           | `evidence=automatic` (solid: produced by the system), `attested` (dashed: declared by a person or a supplier) or `none` (no line)                                                                                                                                                      |
+
+Autonomy, reversibility, reach and usage mode are required for every unit. The three others (identity, control and evidence) are optional.
+
+## Syntax
+
+```
+contour-beta
+  view landscape
+  title Text
+  subtitle "Text"
+  footer "Text"
+  panel "Name"
+    unit ID "Name" level=0 rev=R1 reach=S mode=0
+      action "name" 0
+  supplier ID "Label" "Location" role=model jurisdiction=EU
+```
+
+The keyword is `contour-beta`. Indentation is free. A diagram draws exactly one view.
+
+### Statements
+
+| Statement                                    | Meaning                                                                                                                                                                                       |
+| -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `view <name>`                                | The view to draw: `landscape`, `year`, `supply`, `decisions`, `evidence` or `compare`. Optional: one panel implies `landscape`, two panels imply `compare`.                                   |
+| `title <text>`                               | The title (the common Mermaid title statement; a front-matter `title` also works). `accTitle` and `accDescr` are supported as in other diagrams.                                              |
+| `subtitle "text"`                            | A line under the title. The text is a quoted string.                                                                                                                                          |
+| `footer "text"`                              | A line at the foot of the diagram, for example a source or the word "Illustrative". Repeat the statement for more lines.                                                                      |
+| `panel "Name"`                               | A group of units, normally one organisation. A diagram has at most two panels. Panels may be left out, in which case every unit belongs to one unnamed panel; the two styles cannot be mixed. |
+| `unit ID "Name" key=value ...`               | One AI use. `ID` is a word or a number and must be unique within the diagram (see the year view for the one exception).                                                                       |
+| `action "name" N`                            | An action class of the unit above it, with its autonomy level `N` (0 to 4). Used by the decisions view.                                                                                       |
+| `supplier ID "Label" ["Location"] key=value` | A supplier, with an optional location. Used by the supply view.                                                                                                                               |
+
+### Unit attributes
+
+| Attribute     | Values                                                                      | If omitted          |
+| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |
+| `level`       | `0` to `4`                                                                  | Required            |
+| `rev`         | `R1`, `R2`, `R3`, `R4`                                                      | Required            |
+| `reach`       | `S`, `M`, `L`, `XL`                                                         | Required            |
+| `mode`        | `0` to `5`                                                                  | Required            |
+| `identity`    | `person`, `own`                                                             | `person`            |
+| `policy`      | `enforced`, `planned`, `none`                                               | `none`              |
+| `tier`        | `T0`, `T1`, `T2`, `T3`, `T4`                                                | `T0` (nobody named) |
+| `evidence`    | `automatic`, `attested`, `none`                                             | `none`              |
+| `status`      | `active`, `pilot`, `paused`, `retired`                                      | `active`            |
+| `kinds`       | A comma-separated list of `logs`, `tests`, `gates`, `attestations`          | No kinds            |
+| `hosting`     | `own-premises`, `eu-supplier`, `eea-supplier`, `non-eu-supplier`, `unknown` | `unknown`           |
+| `operated_by` | `self`, `supplier`                                                          | `self`              |
+| `suppliers`   | A comma-separated list of supplier ids                                      | No suppliers        |
+
+### Supplier attributes
+
+| Attribute      | Values                                          | If omitted |
+| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ---------- |
+| `role`         | `model`, `hosting`, `application`, `operations` | Required   |
+| `jurisdiction` | `EU`, `EEA`, `non-EU`                           | Required   |
+
+### Absences are drawn as absences
+
+An attribute that is left out is never guessed. A unit without `policy` has no diamond, a unit without `tier` has no seat, a unit without `evidence` has no baseline, and a unit without `hosting` has hosting `unknown`. The picture therefore shows what is not known or not in place, which is the point of the notation. A value outside the scales above, an unknown attribute, an attribute given twice and a missing required attribute are errors that name the unit.
+
+### Quoting and escaping
+
+Names, labels, locations, subtitles, footers and panel names are quoted strings, in double or single quotes. Inside a string, a backslash escapes the next character, so `\"` is a double quote and `\\` a backslash. Unit and supplier ids are bare words or numbers and cannot hold spaces.
+
+## The six views
+
+### Landscape (V1)
+
+One panel. Every unit is a mark on the grid of autonomy (columns) by reversibility (rows), with all seven dimensions. The top right cell (Level 4 Autonomous, R4 Irreversible) is shaded faintly, because a well-governed landscape has nothing there.
+
+```mermaid-example
+contour-beta
+  view landscape
+  title Three AI uses
+  subtitle "Illustrative"
+  panel "Regional council"
+    unit AS "Case summaries" level=0 rev=R1 reach=M mode=2
+    unit BT "Benefit triage" level=2 rev=R3 reach=XL mode=4 identity=own policy=enforced tier=T2 evidence=automatic
+    unit RT "Roster routing" level=3 rev=R2 reach=L mode=5 identity=own policy=planned tier=T1 evidence=attested
+```
+
+### Year (V2)
+
+Two panels: the landscape at the start of a period and at its end. A unit that changed cell has a trail from its earlier to its later position, a unit that appears only in the second panel is marked new. Units are matched by id, so the year view is the one view where the same id appears in both panels.
+
+```mermaid-example
+contour-beta
+  view year
+  title A year of change
+  panel "2026-01-01"
+    unit A "Case summaries" level=0 rev=R1 reach=M mode=2
+    unit B "Benefit triage" level=1 rev=R2 reach=L mode=4 identity=own
+  panel "2027-01-01"
+    unit A "Case summaries" level=1 rev=R1 reach=L mode=2
+    unit B "Benefit triage" level=2 rev=R3 reach=XL mode=4 identity=own policy=enforced tier=T2
+    unit C "Roster routing" level=3 rev=R2 reach=M mode=5 identity=own
+```
+
+### Supply (V3)
+
+One panel and the suppliers. Marks are placed in containers: the organisation's own boundary for `hosting=own-premises`, a container per supplier otherwise, and a dotted container for jurisdictions outside the EU and the EEA. A unit lists the suppliers it relies on with `suppliers=`, by id.
+
+```mermaid-example
+contour-beta
+  view supply
+  title Who supplies what
+  panel "Regional council"
+    unit A "Case summaries" level=0 rev=R1 reach=M mode=2 hosting=eu-supplier operated_by=supplier suppliers=m1,h1
+    unit B "Benefit triage" level=2 rev=R3 reach=XL mode=4 identity=own hosting=own-premises suppliers=m1
+  supplier m1 "Model provider" "Sweden" role=model jurisdiction=EU
+  supplier h1 "Cloud region" "Finland" role=hosting jurisdiction=EU
+```
+
+### Decisions (V4)
+
+One panel. One row per unit, sorted by level and id, with a bar from Level 0 to the unit's level, the seat with its tier and the policy point. A unit that holds several levels lists its action classes with `action`, each drawn as a thin bar.
+
+```mermaid-example
+contour-beta
+  view decisions
+  title Who decides what
+  panel "Regional council"
+    unit B "Benefit triage" level=2 rev=R3 reach=XL mode=4 identity=own policy=enforced tier=T2
+      action "rank the queue" 0
+      action "flag a case" 1
+      action "request a document" 2
+    unit A "Case summaries" level=0 rev=R1 reach=M mode=2 tier=T1
+```
+
+### Evidence (V5)
+
+One panel. One row per unit and a column per kind of evidence: `logs`, `tests`, `gates`, `attestations`, and none. The kinds a unit lists with `kinds=` are filled for automatic evidence and hatched for attestations.
+
+```mermaid-example
+contour-beta
+  view evidence
+  title Where the proof comes from
+  panel "Regional council"
+    unit B "Benefit triage" level=2 rev=R3 reach=XL mode=4 identity=own evidence=automatic kinds=logs,tests,gates
+    unit C "Roster routing" level=3 rev=R2 reach=L mode=5 identity=own evidence=attested kinds=attestations
+    unit A "Case summaries" level=0 rev=R1 reach=M mode=2
+```
+
+### Compare (V6)
+
+Two panels, two organisations, drawn side by side at identical scales with a shared legend. Nothing is rescaled to fit. Unit ids are unique across the diagram in this view.
+
+```mermaid-example
+contour-beta
+  view compare
+  title Two organisations
+  panel "Regional council"
+    unit A "Case summaries" level=0 rev=R1 reach=M mode=2
+    unit B "Benefit triage" level=2 rev=R3 reach=XL mode=4 identity=own policy=enforced tier=T2
+  panel "Mutual insurer"
+    unit C "Claims triage" level=1 rev=R2 reach=XL mode=4 identity=own policy=enforced tier=T2
+    unit D "Quote engine" level=3 rev=R3 reach=XL mode=5 identity=own policy=planned tier=T3
+```
+
+## Limitations
+
+- **Beta.** The keyword is `contour-beta`, and the syntax may change.
+- **One view per diagram.** A diagram draws the single view named by `view`, or implied by its number of panels. To show several views, write several diagrams.
+- **Fixed palette.** The mode colours and the other colours of the notation come from a fixed palette chosen for colour-vision deficiency, and they do not follow Mermaid themes yet. The mode number is always drawn in the mark, so the diagram never depends on colour alone.
+- **Fixed geometry.** Sizes, scales and layout are fixed so that the diagram can be redrawn by hand and compared; there is no configuration block for them.
+- **At most two panels**, and the year and compare views need exactly two.
+
+## Accessibility
+
+`accTitle` and `accDescr` are supported, as in other Mermaid diagrams:
+
+```mermaid-example
+contour-beta
+  accTitle: One AI use
+  accDescr: A single advisory AI use at the lowest reversibility tier.
+  unit A "Case summaries" level=0 rev=R1 reach=M mode=2
+```
